    "content": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Khaleel Khursheed Ahmed, a tall left-arm fast-medium bowler from Tonk, Rajasthan, has steadily carved a name for himself in Indian cricket with his whippy pace and natural angle across right-handers. Khaleel rose through the ranks quickly, representing India in both ODIs and T20Is before turning into a reliable domestic performer. His accuracy, aggression, and ability to strike in crucial moments have kept him in the conversation for higher honours.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At the <strong>2025 IPL Mega Auction</strong>, Chennai Super Kings invested ₹4.8 crore to secure his services, and he immediately slotted into their bowling attack. Despite CSK enduring a tough season and finishing with the wooden spoon, Khaleel was among the most consistent performers, often giving the team breakthroughs and holding his nerve under pressure. His first season in yellow laid down the foundation for what could be a longer stint at Chepauk.</p>\n\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Personal Details</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Full Name:</strong> Khaleel Khursheed Ahmed</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Date of Birth:</strong> 5 December 1997</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Age:</strong> 27 years (as of October 2025)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Birthplace:</strong> Tonk, Rajasthan, India</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Height:</strong> 1.86 m (6 ft 1 in)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Batting Style:</strong> Right-handed</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bowling Style:</strong> Left-arm fast medium</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Role:</strong> Bowler</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Khaleel Ahmed CSK 2025</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Khaleel Ahmed was one of the rare constants in Chennai Super Kings’ 2025 campaign, featuring in all 14 matches at a time when the team endured its worst-ever season and finished with the wooden spoon. While most of the squad struggled to find rhythm, Khaleel stood out with his work rate, accuracy, and resilience. He ended the season with <strong>137 dot balls</strong>, placing him among the top five bowlers with the most dot deliveries in the tournament, a clear sign of the control he brought despite challenging circumstances. His consistency and commitment to bowling in pressure situations made him one of the few positives for CSK that year. Khaleel wasn’t just a performer in 2025, he became a dependable find and a cornerstone for the franchise’s future campaigns.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Khaleel Ahmed – CSK Stats 2025</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Khaleel’s first season with CSK showed why the franchise had backed him in the auction. He finished as one of the top wicket-takers for the side, displaying consistency even when the team struggled collectively. His fiery spell of 3/29 was a standout performance, and across 14 matches, he remained one of the few bright spots in a difficult campaign.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Season</strong></td><td><strong>Matches</strong></td><td><strong>Wickets</strong></td><td><strong>Total Overs</strong></td><td><strong>Economy</strong></td><td><strong>Average</strong></td><td><strong>Best Bowling</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2025</td><td>14</td><td>15</td><td>46.4</td><td>9.58</td><td>29.8</td><td>3/29</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Khaleel Ahmed International Career</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Khaleel Ahmed made his mark on the international scene in 2018. In September 2018, he was named in India’s ODI squad for the Asia Cup, making his debut against Hong Kong on 18 September 2018. Just weeks later, in October 2018, he was drafted into India’s T20I squad for the home series against the West Indies, where he made his T20I debut on 4 November 2018.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">His ODI career spanned from 2018 to 2019, where he featured in 11 matches. In T20Is, he played from 2018 to 2024, including being named as a reserve player for India in the 2024 ICC Men’s T20 World Cup,a testament to his persistence and relevance in India’s bowling depth.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Though opportunities were limited at the highest level, Khaleel showcased his wicket-taking ability and the left-arm variation that Indian selectors have often looked for.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Khaleel Ahmed – International Bowling Stats</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table aligncenter\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td>ODI</td><td>2018–19</td><td>11</td><td>11</td><td>480</td><td>2</td><td>465</td><td>15</td><td>3/13</td><td>5.81</td><td>31.0</td><td>32.0</td></tr><tr><td>T20I</td><td>2018–24</td><td>18</td><td>18</td><td>396</td><td>1</td><td>562</td><td>16</td><td>2/27</td><td>8.52</td><td>35.1</td><td>24.8</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Format</strong></td><td><strong>Years</strong></td><td><strong>Matches</strong></td><td><strong>Innings</strong></td><td><strong>Balls</strong></td><td><strong>Maidens</strong></td><td><strong>Runs</strong></td><td><strong>Wickets</strong></td><td><strong>Best Bowling</strong></td><td><strong>Economy</strong></td><td><strong>Average</strong></td><td><strong>Strike Rate</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>",
