    "content": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Dewald Brevis didn’t arrive at CSK with a bang. He came in quietly, as a mid-season replacement; no hype, no pressure. But maybe that’s what he needed. At the Mumbai Indians, he was boxed in by expectations. “Baby AB,” they called him, a label too heavy for a boy still figuring things out.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">CSK didn’t ask him to be the next big thing. They just gave him space, and that changed everything.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Under Dhoni’s calm presence and a system built on trust, Brevis stopped playing for approval and started playing for the team. You can see it in his body language: settled, grounded, sharp.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He’s no longer a kid chasing fame. He’s a young man who knows who he is, finally playing his brand of cricket.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And if things keep going this way, CSK won’t just be a chapter, it’ll be his whole book, titled, “The Boy Who Found Himself in Yellow.”</p>\n\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Personal Information</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Full Name: Dewald Tobias Brevis</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Date of Birth: April 29, 2003 (Age: 22)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Birthplace: Johannesburg, South Africa</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Height: 6 ft</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Batting Style: Right-handed</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bowling Style: Right-arm leg-break</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Role: Batting All-rounder</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Nickname: Baby AB / Junior AB</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Brevis CSK Stats</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Match</strong></td><td><strong>Opponent</strong></td><td><strong>Runs</strong></td><td><strong>Balls</strong></td><td><strong>Strike Rate</strong></td><td><strong>Fours</strong></td><td><strong>Sixes</strong></td><td><strong>Result</strong></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>vs SRH</td><td>42</td><td>25</td><td>168.0</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>Lost</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>vs PBKS</td><td>32</td><td>26</td><td>123.1</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>Lost</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>vs RCB</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>0.0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>Lost</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>vs KKR</td><td>52</td><td>25</td><td>208.0</td><td>4</td><td>4</td><td>Won</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>vs RR</td><td>42</td><td>25</td><td>168.0</td><td>3</td><td>3</td><td>Lost</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>vs GT</td><td>57*</td><td>23</td><td>247.8</td><td>2</td><td>5</td><td>Won</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>6 matches</td><td>225 runs</td><td>125 balls</td><td>180.0</td><td>13</td><td>17</td><td>2 wins</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong><em>Tournament Stats: Average: 37.50 | Highest Score: 57* | Half-centuries: 2 | Man of the Match: 1 </em></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Dewald Brevis joined the Chennai Super Kings in April 2025 as a replacement for injured pacer Gurjapneet Singh, signing a contract worth ₹2.2 crore. The move proved transformational for both player and franchise, as CSK&#8217;s belief in youth talent under MS Dhoni&#8217;s mentorship provided Brevis the perfect platform to showcase his explosive batting abilities. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Brevi&#8217;s stats with CSK show his immediate impact. The match-winning performances have made him an indispensable part of the CSK setup.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>International Statistics</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Format</strong></td><td><strong>Matches</strong></td><td><strong>Innings</strong></td><td><strong>Not Out</strong></td><td><strong>Runs</strong></td><td><strong>Highest Score</strong></td><td><strong>Average</strong></td><td><strong>Strike Rate</strong></td><td><strong>100s</strong></td><td><strong>50s</strong></td><td><strong>4s</strong></td><td><strong>6s</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Test</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>84</td><td>51</td><td>28.00</td><td>98.82</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>7</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>ODI</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>1</td><td>110</td><td>49</td><td>22.00</td><td>159.42</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>5</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><td>T20I</td><td>12</td><td>12</td><td>2</td><td>345</td><td>125*</td><td>34.50</td><td>192.73</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>20</td><td>29</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Since making his international debut in August 2023, Dewald Brevis has rapidly established himself as a cornerstone of South Africa&#8217;s white-ball setup. His fearless approach and ability to accelerate scoring in crucial phases have made him indispensable across all formats. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The young batsman&#8217;s recent record-breaking performances, including the highest individual T20I score by a South African (125* vs Australia), demonstrate his evolution from promising talent to match-winning performer on the global stage.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Brevis International Career Highlights:</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Youngest South African to score a T20I century (125* vs Australia, August 2025)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fastest T20I century by a South African (off 52 balls)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Test debut: June 28, 2025, vs Zimbabwe</li>\n\n\n\n<li>ODI debut: August 19, 2025 vs Australia</li>\n\n\n\n<li>T20I debut: August 30, 2023 vs Australia</li>\n</ul>",
